# Dual-machine freeze, catch-up, and PR enforcement

## Standard entries (ALWAYS)

| Host | First file after `git pull` hub `main` |
|------|----------------------------------------|
| **M5** | `docs/M5_READ_ALWAYS.md` |
| **horeb** | `docs/HOREB_READ_ALWAYS.md` |
| **Both** | Umbrella: `docs/DUAL_HOST_SYNC_SYSTEM_SSOT.md` |

On **M5/Mac** (dual-host / freeze / catch-up / pack / fleet):

1. `cd` hub · `git fetch && git switch main && git pull --ff-only`  
2. Read **`docs/M5_READ_ALWAYS.md`** (stable path; freshness + archive fallback)  
3. Run **`./scripts/dual-host-session-start.sh`** (dynamic `gh` scan + local pull; optional `PACK_TARGETS=…`)  
4. Pack + AGENTS: `install-cursor-program-pack.sh` + `dual-host-ensure-agents.sh --write` on open consumers  
5. Static freeze tables alone are **not** enough — live GitHub required  

GitHub: `https://github.com/centexmsp/repository-restructuring/blob/main/docs/M5_READ_ALWAYS.md`

## Other canonical docs (after M5_READ_ALWAYS)

| Doc | Role |
|-----|------|
| `docs/M5_NEXT_STEPS_MASTER_PLAN_2026-07-28.md` | Catch-up, pack/templates, horeb orch lane |
| `docs/DUAL_HOST_SINGLE_GUIDE_2026-07-27.md` | Phases A–D, notify blocks, Phase A record |
